VeilGrid
========

This program is a modified version of "Grid" - An end-to-end encrypted
location-sharing application, Copyright (C) 2024 Chandler Gach
(https://github.com/Rezivure/Grid-Mobile), licensed under the GNU Affero
General Public License, version 3.

Modifications, Copyright (C) 2026 the VeilGrid authors, made from 2026-11-19
onward:

- Removed the Matrix transport, accounts, login, groups, and the associated
  server-side identity. The application no longer talks to a homeserver.
- Added a peer-to-peer transport over Veilid private routes, with a DHT
  rendezvous record as the user's stable address and QR/paste contact linking.
- Added signed, allowlisted, replay-protected location messages; contact
  removal and address rotation; and a hardware-backed identity store with an
  explicit fallback warning.
- Replaced the location history store with a per-address trail sealed using
  AES-256-GCM, with a 7-day retention policy.
- Added saved places with address search, presence, movement alerts, location
  history viewing, and an on-map places layer.
- Added in-app updates from GitHub Releases, replacing store distribution.
- Removed analytics/telemetry endpoints, disabled Android cloud backup, and
  deleted the upstream test, store-deployment, and Matrix integration
  infrastructure.

